# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# recto — environment template (repository root)
#
# recto runs on Cloudflare Workers, so its RUNTIME SECRETS are NOT plain
# environment variables. They live in a Wrangler dev-vars file. Copy that
# template and fill it in:
#
#     cp recto/apps/workers/api/.dev.vars.example recto/apps/workers/api/.dev.vars
#
# That file documents every secret the Worker reads (RECTO_KEK, MAGIC_LINK_SECRET,
# GSC_CLIENT_ID/SECRET, EMAILIT_API_KEY, …). Non-secret service bindings (D1, KV,
# Queues, R2, Vectorize, AI) are declared in recto/apps/workers/api/wrangler.toml.
#
# The only plain process-level variable the tooling reads is below. It is set
# automatically by CI providers (GitHub Actions exports CI=true), so you do not
# normally set it yourself for local development.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Set to "true" in CI to make the Playwright suite fail on `test.only` and
# disable retries-as-success. Left blank locally.
CI=

# ─── Live WordPress integration test (optional) ───
# Only read by the LIVE end-to-end tests (test/wp-live.integration.test.ts and
# recto-ui/tests/live-e2e-fresh.mjs). Those tests skip themselves unless WP_URL
# is set, so leave these blank for normal dev. Use a throwaway post and a fresh
# Application Password.
WP_URL=
WP_USER=
WP_APP_PWD=
WP_SRC_ID=
WP_TARGET_HREF=
WP_MARKER=

# Optional override for the local miniflare D1 sqlite path used by the Playwright
# fixture seeder (recto-ui/tests). Auto-detected from the wrangler state dir by
# default; set this only if your wrangler state lives somewhere non-standard.
RECTO_D1_PATH=
